Yves, Jared,

This is what I had in mind from a mechanism point of view, although I would have thought this be happening within the lavaan object itself once fitted as it is manageable when there is only one or two variables, but when there is 30, 40, 100, 200 degrees of freedom.

One of my models at the moment is of the form Y ~ A + B + C + D + E + F + G resulting in a list of C = [(n + (n-1) + (n-2) + .... + 1] where n = 8, resulting in C = 36 coefficients.

Taking it back to grass roots level, lets say a model is trained, y ~ x, against two data points on the x/y plane, representing (0,0) and (1,1). Obviously this would result in a model describing the formula y = mx + b, where m = 1 and b = 0. I should be able to put in a vector of values for x, (with unknown y), to return another vector of values representing y, so if I put in x = [0.5, 1.5, 3] one would expect it to return y = [0.5, 1.5, 3] which satisfies the originally fitted model without any further training / fitting.

Cheers.

