Yes, I am not sure whether you would like to put the raw data in the function or a set of imputed data. If you want to put raw data, the code should be

out <- runMI(model, data=ex115, fun="growth", m = 5) # You may select MI package from the miPackage argument

If you already have imputed data in a list, the code should be

out <- runMI(model, data=imputedEx115, fun="growth") # imputedEx115 is a list of imputed datasets from any MI packages

